# How I Approach HRBP Work

### 01. Understand the Business

HR decisions should begin with an understanding of the organisation's objectives, operating environment and workforce requirements.

### 02. Identify the People Challenge

Define the actual people problem rather than treating every workforce issue as a generic HR problem.

### 03. Analyse the Evidence

Use workforce data, employee information, business requirements and stakeholder input to understand the situation.

### 04. Build the HR Solution

Develop a practical solution that considers employees, managers, business objectives, cost, risk and implementation.

### 05. Partner With Leaders

Work with managers and business leaders to translate HR strategy into practical action.

### 06. Measure the Outcome

Track relevant metrics to determine whether the intervention is producing the intended result.

### 07. Continuously Improve

Use lessons, data and feedback to improve HR processes and organisational effectiveness.

